<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Exchange from '#src/lib/Exchange.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/app/on-principal',
        '/middleware/signed-in',
        '/middleware/require-role',
        '/ambients/cookies',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/principal.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('set authenticates, the baseline wins, and the caller survives",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/principal.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('clear signs out now and next time, and rotates the caller",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/account/lib/ContactCard.test.ts',
            from: ["test('sales reads the rest of the contact'"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Sign a team member in and out">
        <p><code>principal.set</code> seals the claims into an <code>HttpOnly</code> cookie and
            <code>principal.clear</code> removes it. Both run in a handler, because the cookie is
            written on its answer. Keep the claims small: an id, not the member.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { principal, refuse } from '@abide/abide'
            import { POST } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { TEAM } from './lib/TEAM.server.ts'

            export default POST(async ({ email }: { email: string }) => {
                const member = TEAM.find((one) => one.email === email)
                if (member === undefined) return refuse(401, 'No such account.')
                await principal.set({ id: member.id })
            })
        `} />
        <p>The CRM's, given an email no member has. It is refused, and no cookie is set:</p>
        <Exchange
            method="POST"
            path="/account/signIn"
            body={'{ "email": "nobody@crm.example" }'}
         />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Show the sign-in button that fits the caller">
        <p>Each member of <code>principal</code> is a reactive value. A sign-in or a sign-out
            refreshes what every tab reads, so the button flips with nothing passed to it. The
            <code>name</code> is what your <code>onPrincipal</code> resolved the sealed id to.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { principal } from '@abide/abide'
            import signOut from './signOut.handler.ts'
            import SignIn from './lib/SignIn.abide'
            </script>

            {#if principal.authenticated()}
                <p>{principal.resolved().name}</p>
                <button onclick={() => signOut()}>Sign out</button>
            {:else}
                <SignIn />
            {/if}
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Send the deal value to admins alone">
        <p>Decide in the handler and leave the field out. Hiding it in the template would still
            send it to anyone opening the network panel.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { principal } from '@abide/abide'
            import { GET } from '@abide/abide/server'

            export default GET(async (): Promise<Contact> => {
                const { dealValue, ...rest } = CONTACT
                const { role } = await principal.resolved
                return role === 'admin' ? CONTACT : rest
            })
        `} />
        <p>The CRM's, asked by nobody signed in. The answer has no
            <code>dealValue</code>:</p>
        <Exchange path="/account/getContact" />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Rate limit a browser whether or not anyone signed in">
        <p><code>principal.caller</code> names the browser, not the person. It survives a sign-in
            and is rotated by a sign-out. It is a key, never an identity, and a server read.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { principal, refuse } from '@abide/abide'
            import { GET } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { CONTACTS } from '../contacts/lib/CONTACTS.server.ts'

            const lastExport = new Map<string, number>()

            export default GET(async () => {
                const caller = principal.caller()
                if (Date.now() - (lastExport.get(caller) ?? 0) < 60_000)
                    return refuse(429, 'Try again shortly.')
                lastExport.set(caller, Date.now())
                return CONTACTS
            })
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
